  "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I is a line that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram II does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ lies inside the given subset. But, \n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram III does not represent a subspace. The origin $0=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$  clearly lies outside the subset.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
